---
import CatalogueHeader from "../../components/v2-catalogue/CatalogueHeader.astro";
import FleetField from "@hara-lang/ui-astro/astro/v2/FleetField.astro";
import WwwSpecimen from "../../components/v2/WwwSpecimen.astro";
import DocsSpecimen from "../../components/v2/DocsSpecimen.astro";
import SpecsSpecimen from "../../components/v2/SpecsSpecimen.astro";
import BenchmarksSpecimen from "../../components/v2/BenchmarksSpecimen.astro";
import {
  catalogueGroups,
  catalogueHref,
  catalogueItems,
  catalogueLinkIsExternal,
  catalogueStatusLabels
} from "../../lib/v2-catalogue.mjs";
import "@hara-lang/ui/v2.css";
import "@hara-lang/ui/theme.js";
import "../../styles/v2-lab.css";
import "../../styles/v2-command-retune.css";
import "../../styles/v2-calm-lab.css";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const basePath = base.endsWith("/") ? base : `${base}/`;
const pageUrl = new URL(`${basePath}v2/`, Astro.site);
const socialImage = new URL(`${basePath}og/cards/visual-language.jpg`, Astro.site);
const toolLab = `${basePath}v2/tool/`;
const learnLab = `${basePath}v2/learn/`;
const worldDiscussionLab = `${basePath}v2/world/discussion/`;
const worldAroundLab = `${basePath}v2/world/around/`;
const topLevelItems = catalogueGroups.flatMap((group) => group.items);
const plannedCount = catalogueItems.filter((item) => item.status === "planned").length;
const implementedCount = catalogueItems.filter((item) => item.href).length;
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content="Reference implementation for Hara's shared interface rules and its language, documentation, learning, package, specification, playground, and community routes." />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Hara Visual Language" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Hara visual language v2 reference" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Shared interface rules, reusable specimens, and route-specific examples for the Hara programming language and community." />
    <meta property="og:url" content={pageUrl} />
    <meta property="og:image" content={socialImage} />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="Hara visual language v2 reference" />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content="Interface rules and examples for Hara language, documentation, learning, packages, specifications, tools, and community pages." />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content={socialImage} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={pageUrl} />
    <link rel="icon" href={`${basePath}hara-logo.svg`} type="image/svg+xml" />
    <title>Hara visual language v2 reference</title>
  </head>
  <body class="hara-v2">
    <CatalogueHeader basePath={basePath} activePath="/v2/" />

    <main class="v2-lab-main">
      <section class="v2-lab-hero">
        <div>
          <p class="hara-v2-kicker">Interface reference · Version 2</p>
          <h1>Hara visual language v2</h1>
          <p>This site records the shared interface rules used across Hara and shows how they apply to the language overview, documentation, learning material, packages, specifications, playground, and community. Application pages are specimens for review; they are not product pitches.</p>
          <div class="v2-lab-principles">
            <div><b>Route manifest</b><span>Paths, parent relationships, aliases, and implementation status are recorded in one typed source.</span></div>
            <div><b>Shared rules</b><span>Identity, typography, colour, accessibility, evidence, and common interaction states are documented once.</span></div>
            <div><b>Route examples</b><span>Each language or community route retains its own information architecture and realistic content.</span></div>
            <div><b>Explicit status</b><span>Implemented, reference, historical, and planned material are labelled without implying more than the repository supports.</span></div>
          </div>
          <nav class="v2-lab-quick-links" aria-label="Selected v2 routes">
            <a href={learnLab}><span>Learn</span><strong>Read a first lesson →</strong></a>
            <a href={worldDiscussionLab}><span>World</span><strong>Read community discussion →</strong></a>
            <a href={worldAroundLab}><span>Around Hara</span><strong>View external references →</strong></a>
            <a href={toolLab}><span>Tools</span><strong>Inspect workbench components →</strong></a>
          </nav>
        </div>
        <div class="v2-lab-hero-art"><FleetField title="Hara interface reference field" /></div>
      </section>

      <section class="v2-catalogue-home-intro">
        <div>
          <p class="hara-v2-kicker">Reference structure</p>
          <h2>Shared rules and route-specific examples.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Foundations and Library describe reusable contracts. Language and community routes show how those contracts are applied to Hara's public overview, documentation, learning, packages, specifications, executable examples, and discussion. A planned route links to its implementation issue rather than presenting an empty page.</p>
      </section>

      <div class="v2-catalogue-summary" aria-label="Reference status summary">
        <article><strong>{catalogueGroups.length}</strong><span>reference groups</span></article>
        <article><strong>{topLevelItems.length}</strong><span>top-level references</span></article>
        <article><strong>{plannedCount}</strong><span>planned routes and subroutes</span></article>
        <article><strong>{implementedCount}</strong><span>implemented routes</span></article>
      </div>

      {catalogueGroups.map((group) => (
        <section class="v2-catalogue-family" id={`catalogue-${group.id}`}>
          <header class="v2-catalogue-family-head">
            <div><p class="hara-v2-kicker">Reference group</p><h2>{group.label}</h2></div>
            <p>{group.summary}</p>
          </header>
          <div class="v2-catalogue-card-grid">
            {group.items.map((item) => {
              const external = catalogueLinkIsExternal(item);
              return (
                <article class="v2-catalogue-card" data-status={item.status}>
                  <a
                    href={catalogueHref(item, basePath)}
                    target={external ? "_blank" : undefined}
                    rel={external ? "noreferrer" : undefined}
                  >
                    <span>{item.eyebrow ?? group.label}</span>
                    <h3>{item.label}</h3>
                    <p>{item.summary}</p>
                    <span class="v2-catalogue-status" data-status={item.status}>
                      {catalogueStatusLabels[item.status]}
                      {external && item.issue ? ` · issue #${item.issue}` : ""}
                    </span>
                  </a>
                  {item.children && item.children.length > 0 && (
                    <nav class="v2-catalogue-children" aria-label={`${item.label} routes`}>
                      {item.children.map((child) => {
                        const childExternal = catalogueLinkIsExternal(child);
                        return (
                          <a
                            href={catalogueHref(child, basePath)}
                            target={childExternal ? "_blank" : undefined}
                            rel={childExternal ? "noreferrer" : undefined}
                          >
                            <span>{child.label}</span>
                            <small data-status={child.status}>{catalogueStatusLabels[child.status]}</small>
                          </a>
                        );
                      })}
                    </nav>
                  )}
                </article>
              );
            })}
          </div>
        </section>
      ))}

      <section class="v2-catalogue-legacy-head">
        <div>
          <p class="hara-v2-kicker">Earlier specimens</p>
          <h2>Earlier document layouts remain available for comparison.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>WWW, Docs, Specs, and Benchmarks established the first shared v2 shell. The earlier World example is retained under Learn so that its attribution, discussion, and source-handling decisions can be explained rather than presented as a current destination.</p>
      </section>

      <div class="v2-lab-index" aria-label="Language, community, and interface references">
        <a href={learnLab}><strong>Read Learn</strong><span>Introductory explanations, runnable lessons, projects, and guided interface examples.</span><code>implemented route</code></a>
        <a href={worldDiscussionLab}><strong>Read World discussion</strong><span>Articles, clippings, comments, contributor profiles, presence, and owner-attributed bots.</span><code>implemented route</code></a>
        <a href={worldAroundLab}><strong>View Around Hara</strong><span>External references with source provenance, curation, moderation, and relay review.</span><code>implemented route</code></a>
        <a href={toolLab}><strong>Inspect tool workbenches</strong><span>3D, node, material, and animation editor compositions.</span><code>reference</code></a>
        <a href="https://github.com/hara-lang/visual-language/issues/32"><strong>Catalogue architecture record</strong><span>The completed issue that established the route manifest and application reference structure.</span><code>completed issue #32</code></a>
      </div>

      <WwwSpecimen />
      <DocsSpecimen />
      <SpecsSpecimen />
      <BenchmarksSpecimen />

      <footer class="v2-lab-footer">
        <span>Hara visual language v2 · Editorial contract <a href="https://github.com/hara-lang/visual-language/issues/110">#110</a></span>
        <span><a href={learnLab}>Learn</a> · <a href={worldAroundLab}>Around Hara</a> · <a href={toolLab}>Tool reference</a> · <a href="https://github.com/hara-lang/visual-language/blob/main/V2-EDITORIAL.md">Editorial contract</a> · <a href="https://github.com/hara-lang/visual-language">Source</a></span>
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
